// Control channel between wirefox-panel and the exit-nodes it manages.
//
// The node dials the panel and keeps one Connect stream open for as long as it
// runs, reconnecting with backoff whenever it drops. The panel can't reach the
// nodes (they sit behind NAT, on routers, on Windows desktops), so every
// command travels down this stream.
//
// Transport: gRPC over TLS 1.3. The panel's certificate is self-signed and the
// node pins its SHA-256 fingerprint, which comes from the node key (below).
// TLS SNI is "wirefox-panel".
//
// Authentication: the node sends its secret in the request metadata as
// `authorization: Bearer <secret>`. The panel stores only SHA-256(secret).
//
// Node key: the single string an operator pastes into the node. It is
//
//     "wfx1." + base64url_nopad(JSON)
//
// where the JSON object is
//
//     {"panel": "<host:port of the panel's gRPC listener>",
//      "fp":    "<hex SHA-256 of the panel's certificate>",
//      "secret":"<hex, 32 random bytes>"}
//
// Conversation:
//   1. node -> Hello
//   2. panel -> Welcome, then the node's current TunnelConfig
//   3. node -> Status every Welcome.status_interval_secs, and right away when
//      its tunnel state changes
//   4. panel -> TunnelConfig whenever the operator changes it, and Command
//      whenever one is issued; the node answers each Command with a
//      CommandResult carrying the same id.
